structural_finding sf:two-bitmap-implementations
  finding two independent bitmap admission implementations exist and appear unaware of each other
  implementation_a canonical estate scaling_substrate/hot_index.py with SparseBitmap, ExecutableClosureIndex and a native ROBDD, 3 checks passing
  implementation_b current source address_plane.py with BitRegistry and authority/capability masks, exercised by its own tests
  significance the exact-filter stage of the optimization cascade has two physical candidates and no binding between them
  action the semantic query optimizer's physical plan catalog should carry both, measured, before either is treated as the implementation

